Jon Stevenson <steve203@msu.edu> writes:


And in Russian, the preposition "po" can mean apparently just about 

> anything.
> 
> 

hmmm, in over 25 years of knowing russian, i never had that feeling, and 
still don't.  russian "po" has lots of meanings, but they are still precise 
meanings, not interchangeable with other prepositions.  one of the advantages of 
selmaho BAI is that the words in BAI usually have a direct connection to a brivla 
with the intended meaning, and so they are easier to learn and remember.
stevo
           
